# Exercise the API from VS Code (REST Client extension: click "Send Request").
# Start the API first: `make api` (local mode, in-memory).

@host = http://localhost:8000
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Health
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Artisan: create a listing (returns an UploadTicket)
# @name create
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hand-thrown clay mug",
  "description": "Wheel-thrown and glazed by hand.",
  "price": 450,
  "tags": ["pottery", "kitchen"],
  "artisan_name": "Meera"
}

### Local mode: pretend the upload finished (marks the video ready)
POST {{api}}/products/{{create.response.body.product.id}}/upload-complete

### Buyer: search by keyword
GET {{api}}/products?q=clay

### Buyer: filter by tag
GET {{api}}/products?tag=pottery

### Buyer: product details
GET {{api}}/products/{{create.response.body.product.id}}

### Buyer: place an order
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{create.response.body.product.id}}",
  "buyer_name": "Ravi",
  "quantity": 2
}
